>
> I don't like polypiling, but I also don't like heaps of jumk all over
> the dungeon floor.  Is there a way to destroy objects you don't want?

If all you want to do is make them invisible: dig a pit,
put as much as you want in the pit, roll a boulder to
fill the pit.

The objects will still exist, so this method will be
insufficient for a pudding farming game or maybe for an
extinctionist game, but most games under 500K moves
don't create so many items that matters.

Polypiling is the fastest way to make a large number of
objects cease to exist and stop making up memory and
disk space, but others have posted an assortment of
other methods so I only gave the common cosmetic one.



